      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Multiple Choice Questions"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "1. A computer network is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) A single computer system",
              "(b) A group of connected computers and devices",
              "(c) A software program",
              "(d) A storage device"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "2. The device used to connect a computer to a network is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Monitor",
              "(b) Keyboard",
              "(c) Network Interface Card (NIC)",
              "(d) Printer"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "3. A network that covers a small geographical area, such as a school or office, is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) WAN",
              "(b) MAN",
              "(c) LAN",
              "(d) Internet"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "4. The topology that uses a central hub or switch is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Bus Topology",
              "(b) Ring Topology",
              "(c) Star Topology",
              "(d) Mesh Topology"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "5. The OSI model contains:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Five layers",
              "(b) Six layers",
              "(c) Seven layers",
              "(d) Eight layers"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "6. The protocol mainly used to view web pages is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) FTP",
              "(b) DNS",
              "(c) TCP",
              "(d) HTTP"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "7. The main function of a router is to:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Store data",
              "(b) Connect devices within a network",
              "(c) Connect different networks",
              "(d) Display web pages"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "8. DNS is used to:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Transfer files",
              "(b) Protect data",
              "(c) Convert domain names into IP addresses",
              "(d) Connect hardware devices"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "9. The device that converts digital signals for Internet transmission is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Switch",
              "(b) Hub",
              "(c) Modem",
              "(d) NIC"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "10. The topology that provides the highest reliability is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Bus topology",
              "(b) Ring topology",
              "(c) Star topology",
              "(d) Mesh topology"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Short Questions"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "What is a computer network?",
              "Write two uses of computer networks.",
              "What is network architecture?",
              "Name any two components of a computer network.",
              "What is the OSI model?",
              "Write the name of any two network topologies.",
              "What is a Local Area Network (LAN)?",
              "What is the function of a router?",
              "What is a network protocol?",
              "What is the purpose of DNS?"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Long Questions"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "Define a computer network. Explain its importance and uses in daily life.",
              "Explain network architecture and describe the main components of a computer network.",
              "What is the OSI model? Explain its layers and their functions.",
              "Define network topology. Explain bus, star, ring, and mesh topologies with advantages and disadvantages.",
              "Explain the types of computer networks. Describe LAN, WAN, and the Internet.",
              "Describe the main networking devices used in a computer network and explain their functions.",
              "What are network protocols? Explain TCP/IP, HTTP, FTP, and DNS.",
              "Explain IP addressing. Describe IPv4, IPv6, the default gateway, and subnetting."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
